From 6d6d18cfd5ba4e3b59cbbe90ede8c96d1bd1f8b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:57:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 38/87] h713: deep sleep switches off by default, deep = D1a,
 board id and test bit

The two deep steps 0034 put under a switch still defaulted to on, so
every "deep" defconfig built the variant the reviews say must not run
(PRUEFUNG5 DEEP-01, design A of the release design: never reset
VDD_SYS in a suspend). H713_DEEP_VDD_SYS and H713_DEEP_PLL_LDO are now
off by default; the LDO step also needs the new H713_HOSC_IS_DCXO,
which says the 24 MHz clock does not come through the PLL domain - no
board is confirmed and no product defconfig sets it (DEEP-08).

h713_hy310_deep_defconfig is now the same as the D1a one, with the
"is not set" lines spelled out, and so is the HY300 Pro deep
defconfig. h713_hy310_deep_blobparity_defconfig keeps both steps on,
only for the trace comparison with the blob that refuted DEEP-01; its
trace equals the 0033 deep trace, the deep trace equals the 0034 D1a
trace.

The help texts say what deep sleep does (DEEP-06): root clocks and
PLLs off, LOSC as found, the MBUS rebuild; LDO and VDD_SYS only with
their switches. RAILS_PIN has no user and says so; the PLATFORM_H713
help no longer claims there is no self-refresh (CS-17). r-ccu.c names
the RE note behind the VDD_SYS condition instead of a guess (DEEP-02).

New: H713_BOARD_ID (1 HY310, 2 HY300 Pro) in BUILD2 15..12, and
H713_TEST, a test build in build word bit 30.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
